Package: agentic-memory
Version: __VERSION__
Section: devel
Priority: optional
Architecture: __ARCH__
Depends: libc6, libgcc-s1 | libgcc1, libstdc++6, zlib1g, ca-certificates, libgssapi-krb5-2, libssl3t64 | libssl3 | libssl1.1, libicu76 | libicu74 | libicu72 | libicu71 | libicu70 | libicu69 | libicu68 | libicu67 | libicu66 | libicu63 | libicu60
Maintainer: Aaron Lionheart <lionheartaaron@gmail.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/lionheartaaron/agentic-memory
Description: Local memory and code intelligence server for AI agents
 Agentic Memory gives an AI assistant a memory that persists between
 conversations, and a symbol-level understanding of the codebases it is
 pointed at. It runs as a local server, speaks MCP and a REST API, and
 serves its own dashboard.
 .
 Everything stays on the machine it runs on. Embeddings are computed
 locally with ONNX Runtime, C# is analysed with Roslyn and TypeScript
 with the real TypeScript compiler hosted in V8.
 .
 The .NET runtime is bundled, so nothing else needs installing. Model
 weights are not: the embedding model downloads on first run into
 $XDG_DATA_HOME/agentic-memory/models.
